      "value": "@{5fcd676570b59138e6ef0271|full_name}: In some situations crunch might not be necessary. \n\nI'm pretty sure unity editor would list crunched size for a crunched texture, in the preview. I had an avatar over 10mb with ASTC 6x6 and I took that as an opportunity to compare. 0.6 MB in ASTC but 0.7 MB in ETC. Converted three textures to ETC and got in the limit.\n\nSince quest avatars build so quickly I just brute forced it. I would like to see SDK limit increased such that it won't tell me that my bundle of 10.00MB is over 10.00MB and therefore too large. I don't mind if 10.01MB is too large...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
