  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I agree with the new update to force ASTC on all textures for avatars. The problem that I have is that now due to this update the size of my images has increased, so now I have to manually edit all of the textures on my avatar to be able to upload it once again to quest because it has to fit within the measly 10 MB quest limit. I noticed that after the update the size of textures has increased by around 30%. This is due to the fact that DXT1 (which I was using previously as it was the default) can be compressed more than ASTC at the same resolution. This essentially means that I need to remake all old avatars that had lots of detail in order to be able to upload them again. The easiest solution that I see is to increase the size limitation on quest by 30% or more to 13MB+. I think I'm not the only one who did it this way and I think a lot of people will be upset once they update their avatars and find out they won't be able to upload them anymore without more work and a possible change in quality.",
